  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 893047,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "monerod `--restricted-zmq-rpc` does not enforce the same request restrictions as restricted HTTP RPC.\n\nRestricted ZMQ relies primarily on a small method blocklist, so several allowed methods can still accept requests that restricted HTTP explicitly rejects or caps. Confirmed examples include `get_output_histogram` and `get_output_keys`.\n\nThis can allow externally exposed restricted ZMQ endpoints to bypass intended resource limits, leading to availability issues.\n\nResolved in https://github.com/monero-project/monero/pull/10424 and v0.18.5.0.",
